      "summary": ": Summary Saturday 25/07 We are open today, We have received 3-5 cm of wind effected snow with some good drifting in places. We are forecasted for a fine day ahead, Although currently we are seeing some snow showers with mountain fog, this is due to clear up this morning. We have had a rime night. this means it will be an operationally challenging morning for us. Expect possible delays on lifts and terrain. Chains on 2WD's from chain bay 1 and 4wds form heil corner. Main Basin and Valley View lifts scheduled to open from 08:30am. White star, Captains, T-Bar, Willows and Soho to follow with delays due to rime. The team is working hard to get us open as soon as possible.",
